	⟪(a)⟫ of persons, either as arriving or returning from elsewhere: ⟦Matthew 8:9|Mt 8:9⟧, ⟦Mark 6:31|Mk 6:31⟧, ⟦Luke 7:8|Lk 7:8⟧, ⟦John 4:27|Jo 4:27⟧, ⟦Romans 9:9|Ro 9:9⟧, al.; seq. ἀπό, ⟦Mark 5:35|Mk 5:35⟧ ⟦Mark 7:1|7:1⟧, ⟦John 3:2|Jo 3:2⟧, al.; ἐκ, ⟦Luke 5:17|Lk 5:17⟧, ⟦John 3:31|Jo 3:31⟧, al.; εἰς, ⟦Mark 1:29|Mk 1:29⟧, al.; διά seq. εἰς, ⟦Mark 7:31|Mk 7:31⟧; ἐν (Cremer, 263 f., but v.s. ἐν), ⟦Romans 15:29|Ro 15:29⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:21|I Co 4:21⟧; ἐπί, c. acc., ⟦Mark 6:53|Mk 6:53⟧ ⟦Mark 11:13|11:13⟧, ⟦John 19:33|Jo 19:33⟧, al.; κατά, c. acc., ⟦Luke 10:33|Lk 10:33⟧ ⟦Acts 16:7|Ac 16:7⟧; παρά, c. gen., ⟦Luke 8:49|Lk 8:49⟧; c. acc., ⟦Matthew 15:29|Mt 15:29⟧, ⟦Mark 9:14|Mk 9:14⟧, al.; c. dat. comm., incomm. (M, Pr., 75, 245), ⟦Matthew 21:5|Mt 21:5⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:5|Re 2:5⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:16|16⟧; with adverbs: πόθεν, ⟦John 3:8|Jo 3:8⟧, al.; ἄνωθεν, ⟦John 3:31|Jo 3:31⟧; ὄπισθεν, ⟦Mark 5:27|Mk 5:27⟧; ὧδε, ⟦Matthew 8:29|Mt 8:29⟧; ἐκεῖ, ⟦John 18:3|Jo 18:3⟧; ποῦ, ⟦Hebrews 11:8|He 11:8⟧; seq. ἕως, ⟦Luke 4:42|Lk 4:42⟧; ἄχρι, ⟦Acts 11:5|Ac 11:5⟧; with purpose expressed by inf., ⟦Mark 5:14|Mk 5:14⟧, ⟦Luke 1:59|Lk 1:59⟧, al.; by fut. ptcp., ⟦Matthew 27:49|Mt 27:49⟧; ἵνα, ⟦John 12:9|Jo 12:9⟧; εἰς τοῦτο, ἵνα, ⟦Acts 9:21|Ac 9:21⟧; διά, c. acc., ⟦John 12:9|Jo 12:9⟧; before verbs of action, ἔρχεται καί, ἦλθε καί, etc.: ⟦Mark 2:18|Mk 2:18⟧, ⟦John 6:15|Jo 6:15⟧, al.; ἔρχου καὶ ἴδε, ⟦John 1:47|Jo 1:47⟧ ⟦John 11:34|11:34⟧; ἐλθών (redundant; Dalman, Words, 20 f.), ⟦Matthew 2:8|Mt 2:8⟧ ⟦Matthew 8:7|8:7⟧, ⟦Mark 7:25|Mk 7:25⟧, ⟦Acts 16:39|Ac 16:39⟧, al.; similarly ἐρχόμενος, ⟦Luke 15:25|Lk 15:25⟧, al.; of coming into public view: esp. of the Messiah (ὁ ἐρχόμενος, ⟦Matthew 11:3|Mt 11:3⟧, al.; v. Cremer, 264), ⟦Luke 3:16|Lk 3:16⟧, ⟦John 4:25|Jo 4:25⟧; hence, of Jesus, ⟦Matthew 11:19|Mt 11:19⟧, ⟦Luke 7:34|Lk 7:34⟧, ⟦John 5:43|Jo 5:43⟧, al.; of the second coming, ⟦Matthew 10:23|Mt 10:23⟧, ⟦Acts 1:11|Ac 1:11⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:5|I Co 4:5⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:2|I Th 5:2⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ of time: ἔρξονται ἡμέραι (pres. for fut.: Bl., §56, 8), ⟦Luke 23:29|Lk 23:29⟧, ⟦Hebrews 8:8|He 8:8⟧ (LXX); fut., ⟦Matthew 9:15|Mt 9:15⟧, ⟦Mark 2:20|Mk 2:20⟧, al.; ἔρξεται ὥρα, ὅτε, ⟦John 4:21|Jo 4:21⟧, ⟦John 4:23|23⟧. al.; ἦλθεν, ἐλήλυθε ἡ ὥρα, ⟦John 13:1|Jo 13:1⟧ ⟦John 16:32|16:32⟧ 17:1; ἡ ἡμέρα τ. κυρίου, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:2|I Th 5:2⟧; καιροί, ⟦Acts 3:19|Ac 3:19⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of things and events: κατακλυσμός, ⟦Luke 17:27|Lk 17:27⟧; λιμός, ⟦Acts 7:11|Ac 7:11⟧; ἡ ὀργή, ⟦1 Thessalonians 1:10|I Th 1:10⟧; ὁ λύχνος, ⟦Mark 4:21|Mk 4:21⟧ (v. Swete, in l.). Metaph., τ. ἀγαθά, ⟦Romans 3:8|Ro 3:8⟧; τ. τέλειον, ⟦1 Corinthians 13:10|I Co 13:10⟧; ἡ πίστις, ⟦Galatians 3:23|Ga 3:23⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:25|25⟧; ἡ ἐντολή, ⟦Romans 7:9|Ro 7:9⟧; with prepositions: ἐκ τ. θλίψεως, ⟦Revelation 7:14|Re 7:14⟧; ἐις τ. χεῖρον, ⟦Mark 5:26|Mk 5:26⟧; εἰς πειρασμόν, ⟦Mark 14:38|ib. 14:38⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to go⟫: ὀπίσω, c. gen. (Heb. ⁨הָלַךְ אַחֲרֵי⁩), ⟦Matthew 16:24|Mt 16:24⟧, ⟦Mark 8:34|Mk 8:34⟧, ⟦Luke 9:23|Lk 9:23⟧; σύν, ⟦John 21:3|Jo 21:3⟧; ὁδόν, ⟦Luke 2:44|Lk 2:44⟧. (Cf. ἀν-, ἐπ-αν-, ἀπ-, δι-, εἰς, ἐπ-εἰσ-, παρ-εἰσ-, συν-εἰσ-, ἐξ-, δι-εξ-, ἐπ-, κατ-, παρ-, ἀντι-παρ-, περι-, προ-, προσ-, συν-έρχομαι.)
SYN.: πορεύομαι, χωρέω (v, Thayer, s.v. ἔρξομαι).

G2078.b:
⟪ἔσχατος⟫, -η, -ον
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אַחֲרִית⁩ ⁨אַחֲרוֹן⁩ ;] ⟪last, utmost, extreme⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of place: of the lowest or least honoured place, ⟦Luke 14:9|Lk 14:9⟧, ⟦Luke 14:10|10⟧; τ. ἔσχατον, c. gen. part., ⟦Acts 1:8|Ac 1:8⟧ ⟦Acts 13:47|13:47⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of time: ⟦Matthew 20:12|Mt 20:12⟧, ⟦Matthew 20:14|14⟧, ⟦Mark 12:6|Mk 12:6⟧, ⟦Mark 12:22|22⟧, opp. to πρῶτος, ⟦Matthew 20:8|Mt 20:8⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:45|I Co 15:45⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:19|Re 2:19⟧, al.; τὰ ἔ. καὶ τ. πρῶτα, ⟦Matthew 12:45|Mt 12:45⟧, ⟦Luke 11:26|Lk 11:26⟧, ⟦2 Peter 2:20|II Pe 2:20⟧; of the Eternal, ὁ πρῶτος καὶ ὁ ἔ., ⟦Revelation 1:17|Re 1:17⟧ ⟦Revelation 2:8|2:8⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:13|22:13⟧; in phrases relating to the Messianic age and the consummation of the Kingdom of God: ἐπ’ ἐσχάτου (-ων) τ. ἡμερῶν, ⟦Hebrews 1:2|He 1:2⟧, ⟦2 Peter 3:3|II Pe 3:3⟧; τ. χρόνων, ⟦1 Peter 1:20|I Pe 1:20⟧; ἔ. ὥρα, ⟦1 John 2:18|I Jo 2:18⟧; ἐπ’ ἐ. χόνου, ⟦Jude 1:18|Ju 18⟧; ἐν ἐ. ἡμέραις, ⟦Acts 2:17|Ac 2:17⟧, ⟦James 5:3|Ja 5:3⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 3:1|II Ti 3:1⟧; neut., ἔσχατον, as adv., ⟦Mark 12:22|Mk 12:22⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:8|I Co 15:8⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of rank: ⟦Mark 9:35|Mk 9:35⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:9|I Co 4:9⟧

G2087.b:
⟪ἕτερος⟫, -α, -ον,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אַחֵר⁩ ;] distributive pron., prop. dual (Bl., §13, 5; 51, 6), denoting the second of a pair, but in late Gk. encroaching on ἄλλος (M, Pr., 79 f.);
⟪1.⟫ of number, ⟪other⟫; c. art., ⟪the other⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of two, ⟦Luke 5:7|Lk 5:7⟧ ⟦Luke 9:56|9:56⟧, al.; opp. to ὁ πρῶτος, ⟦Matthew 21:30|Mt 21:30⟧; ὁ εἷς, ⟦Matthew 6:24|Mt 6:24⟧, ⟦Luke 7:41|Lk 7:41⟧, ⟦Acts 23:6|Ac 23:6⟧, al.; ἕ. μὲν . . . ἕ. δέ, ⟪the one . . . the other⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 15:40|I Co 15:40⟧; ⟪the next⟫: ⟦Luke 6:6|Lk 6:6⟧ ⟦Luke 9:56|9:56⟧ (sc. ἡμέρα, Xen.), ⟦Acts 20:15|Ac 20:15⟧ ⟦Acts 27:3|27:3⟧; = ὁ πλησίον, ⟪one's neighbour⟫: ⟦Romans 2:1|Ro 2:1⟧ ⟦Romans 13:8|13:8⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 6:1|I Co 6:1⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ of more than two, ⟪another⟫: ⟦Matthew 8:21|Mt 8:21⟧ ⟦Matthew 11:3|11:3⟧, ⟦Luke 6:6|Lk 6:6⟧ ⟦Luke 22:65|22:65⟧, ⟦John 19:37|Jo 19:37⟧, ⟦Romans 8:39|Ro 8:39⟧, al.; pl., ⟦Acts 2:13|Ac 2:13⟧; οἱ μὲν . . . ἄλλοι δὲ . . . ἕ. δέ, ⟦Matthew 16:14|Mt 16:14⟧; τινὲς . . . ἕ. δέ, ⟦Luke 11:16|Lk 11:16⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of kind or quality, ⟪other, another, different⟫ (Plat., Dem., al.): ⟦Mark 16:12|Mk 16:[12]⟧, ⟦Luke 9:29|Lk 9:29⟧, ⟦Acts 2:4|Ac 2:4⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:21|I Co 14:21⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:4|II Co 11:4⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:6|Ga 1:6⟧, al. (cf. ἑτερό-γλωσσος, -διδασκαλέω, -ζυγέω).
SYN.: ἄλλος, q.v. (v. reff. ut supr., also Robertson, Gr., 748 ff.).

G2089.b:
⟪ἔτι⟫ adv., ⟪yet, as yet, still⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of time;
⟪(a)⟫ of the present (adhuc): ⟦Mark 5:35|Mk 5:35⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:3|I Co 3:3⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 15:17|15:17⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:10|Ga 1:10⟧, al.;
⟪(b)⟫ of the past, mostly c. impf.: ⟦Matthew 12:46|Mt 12:46⟧, ⟦Luke 8:49|Lk 8:49⟧ ⟦Luke 15:20|15:20⟧, ⟦John 20:1|Jo 20:1⟧, ⟦Acts 9:1|Ac 9:1⟧, ⟦Romans 5:6|Ro 5:6⟧, ⟦Romans 5:8|8⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:5|II Th 2:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:10|He 7:10⟧ ⟦Hebrews 9:8|9:8⟧, al.;
⟪(c)⟫ of the future: ⟦Luke 1:15|Lk 1:15⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:10|II Co 1:10⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ with a neg.: ⟦Matthew 5:13|Mt 5:13⟧, ⟦Luke 16:2|Lk 16:2⟧ ⟦Luke 20:36|20:36⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:2|He 10:2⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:12|Re 3:12⟧ ⟦Revelation 20:3|20:3⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ Of degree, ⟪even, yet, still, further⟫: c. compar., ⟦Philippians 1:9|Phl 1:9⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:15|He 7:15⟧; of what remains, ⟦Mark 12:6|Mk 12:6⟧, ⟦John 4:35|Jo 4:35⟧ ⟦John 7:33|7:33⟧, al.; of what is added, ⟦Matthew 18:16|Mt 18:16⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:65|26:65⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:32|He 11:32⟧ ⟦Hebrews 12:26|12:26⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:27|27⟧; of con­tinuance apart from the idea of time, ⟦Romans 3:7|Ro 3:7⟧ ⟦Romans 6:2|6:2⟧ ⟦Romans 9:19|9:19⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:11|Ga 5:11⟧; ἔτι δἐ, ⟦Acts 2:26|Ac 2:26⟧ (LXX), ⟦Hebrews 11:36|He 11:36⟧; ἔτι τε καί, ⟦Luke 14:26|Lk 14:26⟧, ⟦Acts 21:28|Ac 21:28⟧

G2090.b:
⟪ἑτοιμάζω⟫
(< ἕτοιμος), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨כּוּן⁩ hi. (Hatch, Essays, 51 ff.) ;] to prepare, make ready;
⟪(a)⟫ absol., of hospitable preparation: ⟦Mark 14:15|Mk 14:15⟧, ⟦Luke 9:52|Lk 9:52⟧ ⟦Luke 12:47|12:47⟧ ⟦Luke 22:9|22:9⟧, ⟦Luke 22:12|12⟧; c. inf., ⟦Matthew 26:17|Mt 26:17⟧; ἵνα, ⟦Mark 14:12|Mk 14:12⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ c. acc rei: ⟦Matthew 22:4|Mt 22:4⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:19|26:19⟧, ⟦Mark 14:16|Mk 14:16⟧, ⟦Luke 12:20|Lk 12:20⟧ ⟦Luke 17:8|17:8⟧ ⟦Luke 22:8|22:8⟧, ⟦Luke 22:13|13⟧ ⟦Luke 23:56|23:56⟧ ⟦Luke 24:1|24:1⟧, ⟦John 14:2|Jo 14:2-3⟧, ⟦Philemon 1:22|Phm 22⟧, ⟦Revelation 9:7|Re 9:7⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:12|16:12⟧; seq. εἰς, ⟦2 Timothy 2:21|II Ti 2:21⟧; of God's ordaining coming events (Dalman, Words, 128); of blessing, ⟦Matthew 20:23|Mt 20:23⟧ ⟦Matthew 25:34|25:34⟧, ⟦Mark 10:40|Mk 10:40⟧, ⟦Luke 2:31|Lk 2:31⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:9|I Co 2:9⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:16|He 11:16⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:6|Re 12:6⟧; of judgment, ⟦Matthew 25:41|Mt 25:41⟧; of preparation for the Messiah, τ. ὁδὸν κυρίου, ⟦Matthew 3:3|Mt 3:3⟧, ⟦Mark 1:3|Mk 1:3⟧, ⟦Luke 1:76|Lk 1:76⟧ ⟦Luke 3:4|3:4⟧ (LXX);
⟪(c)⟫ c. acc pers.: ⟦Luke 1:17|Lk 1:17⟧, ⟦Acts 23:23|Ac 23:23⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:7|Re 19:7⟧, seq. ἵνα, ⟦Revelation 8:6|Re 8:6⟧; εἰς, ⟦2 Timothy 2:21|II Ti 2:21⟧, ⟦Revelation 9:7|Re 9:7⟧, ⟦Revelation 9:15|15⟧ ⟦Revelation 21:2|21:2⟧.†

G2092.b:
⟪ἕτοιμος⟫, -ον also (in cl. after Thuc.) -η (⟦2 Corinthians 9:5|II Co 9:5⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:5|I Pe 1:5⟧), -ον,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨כּוּן⁩, ⁨מָכוֹן⁩ (cf. Hatch, Essays, 51 ff.) ;] ⟪prepared, ready⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of things: ⟦Matthew 22:4|Mt 22:4⟧, ⟦Matthew 22:8|8⟧, ⟦Mark 14:15|Mk 14:15⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 9:5|II Co 9:5⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 10:16|10:16⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:5|I Pe 1:5⟧; ἔρχεσθε ὅτι ἤδη ἕτοιμά ἐστιν (Field, Notes, 67), ⟦Luke 14:17|Lk 14:17⟧; ὁ καιρός, ⟦John 7:6|Jo 7:6⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of persons: ⟦Matthew 24:44|Mt 24:44⟧ ⟦Matthew 25:10|25:10⟧, ⟦Luke 12:40|Lk 12:40⟧, ⟦Acts 23:21|Ac 23:21⟧; seq. πρός, ⟦Titus 3:1|Tit 3:1⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:15|I Pe 3:15⟧; c. inf., ⟦Luke 22:23|Lk 22:23⟧; τοῦ, c. inf. (WM, § 44, 4a; Robertson, Gr., 1068), ⟦Acts 23:15|Ac 23:15⟧; ἐν ἑ. ἔχω (MM, Exp., xiv), c. inf., ⟦2 Corinthians 10:6|II Co 10:6⟧.†

G2099.b:
*† ⟪εὐαγγελιστής⟫, -οῦ, ὁ ⟪an evangelist⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in NT, a preacher of the gospel: ⟦Acts 21:8|Ac 21:8⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:11|Eph 4:11⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 4:5|II Ti 4:5⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ later, a writer of a gospel (eccl.).†
